 "web": "These barriers land on the same person at once. One homeowner: in her seventies, disabled after years of work that was hard on the body; her house is a mobile home on the only flat ground, beside a creek that flooded twice in three years; it has no flood insurance because the premium would be a month's income and the map said she was safe; her coverage is Medicaid and Medicare; her income is a disability or retirement check that would shrink if she earned more; she is raising a great-grandchild because addiction took the generation in between; the porch steps she cannot climb are rotting, and there is no carpenter nearby she could afford if there were one. No one barrier decided her life. Together they set the price.",
