   "plain": "For a century, coal decided what work paid here, who built the roads and hospitals, and what young people planned to do. Coal employment fell steeply; the jobs that replaced it are mostly in health care, schools and retail, much of it paid for by public money. Many young people leave to find work, and the county shrinks.",
