   "plain": "A large share of adults here live with a disability, often from work that broke the body or from age. For many families, a disability check (SSDI or SSI) is the steadiest income in the household. The rules are strict and nearly all-or-nothing: earn more than a set monthly amount and the benefit can stop — so a person who could work a little often can't risk it.",
