 "theology": {
  "readings": [
   "**The Catholic Bishops of Appalachia, *This Land Is Home to Me* (1975).** ⚠️ A pastoral letter from the bishops of the Appalachian region, written in the voice of the mountains — part prose, part poem — about coal, absentee ownership, powerlessness and the dignity of mountain people, and asking the Church to listen to the poor and learn from them. It stands without the course: read the opening section aloud before the first work day.",
   "**The Catholic Bishops of Appalachia, *At Home in the Web of Life* (1995).** ⚠️ The twentieth-anniversary letter: sustainable communities, care for the land and the people together. Pair with the flood (Barrier 2) and the land (Barrier 3)."
  ],
  "question": "The people on this porch have been told for sixty years — by presidents, photographers and bestsellers — who they are. This week, can I build the ramp and let them tell me instead?"
 },
